# <%= app_title %>

> A SaaS application built with [Magik](https://github.com/developerz-ai/magik) — one Ruby DSL for models, screens, actions, jobs, ledgers and APIs, server-rendered as HTML plus htmx with no frontend framework and no build step. Multi-tenant by default with `tenant_id` auto-scoping and UUIDv7 keys; money is integer cents; an action is the only thing that mutates, a job the only thing that runs async, a ledger the only thing that moves money, and a screen never queries the database. Those rules are enforced at boot, each failure carrying a stable `MAGIK_*` code, a cause and a runnable `fix:`. Generated by `magik new` with magik `<%= magik_version %>` on `<%= generated_on %>`.

This file is a link map, not a status page. **It states no version, count or verdict without the command that resolves it** — a number written here goes stale on the next commit and the command does not.

**The one fact you must not get wrong:** magik `<%= magik_version %>` is a **RubyGems name reservation**. The framework is not implemented, so **this app cannot run**. Every declaration in `app/` is a design artefact that has never been parsed. Resolve it before quoting anything else here:

