magik help               # every command, marked ready or planned
```

## Read the DSL locally, not on the web

**The Magik DSL is not in your training data.** `model`, `screen`, `action`, `ledger`, `channel`, `flow`, `component` — none of it. Written from memory it comes out Rails-shaped and wrong.

The gem ships its own documentation. It is on disk, it is instant, and it is the documentation for **the exact magik version this app has** — which no web page can promise, because a web page tracks `main` and your gem does not.

```bash
magik docs path            # the docs directory. Point your normal grep/glob/read tools at it
magik docs list            # every page and its slug
magik docs search ledger   # find the page before you guess the API
magik docs Models          # read one page
```

`magik docs path` is the one that matters most: it turns the shipped docs into ordinary files your existing search already reaches, which beats any CLI output format.

The same pages are at <https://github.com/developerz-ai/magik/wiki> — the fallback, for a human in a browser.

## Resolve before you quote

- `magik version --json` · `magik help` — what this app's gem actually is, and which commands run.
- `magik docs list` — every documentation page available locally, with its slug.
- `magik check --json` — every boot guardrail, as findings with code, cause, fix and location. **The authoritative answer to "is this app correct".** Planned.
- `magik check --scale` — queries with no `tenant_id` predicate. `--domains` for boundary violations, `--components` for what shadows what.
- `magik test --json` — the suite. Planned.
- `magik routes` — every route the naming convention produced. There is no route file.
- `magik domains --json` — the domain graph: nodes, edges, exposures, events. **The authoritative domain map** — `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` carries the reasoning, this carries the fact.
- `magik errors explain <CODE> --json` — what a `MAGIK_*` code means and the command that fixes it.
- `ls app/actions/` — the complete list of writes in this product. If that is not true, it is a bug.

